# P108 on Windows GtkBackend (TEST_BACKEND=gtk4): a held drag, then a throw, after the app's own FREE and BOUND.
# The GTK window is not scaled (scale 1.0): the card is 40x40 at frame x 34-74, y 153-193 px (capture of 2026-10-19).
# HOLD comes FIRST, from where STEPS DONE leaves the card (offset 0): press its centre, drag 20, hold 0.3 s, release in
# place. Pass: a DRAG release 20 on with velocity 0 and HOLD, no coast. The card is then at offset 20, a known place.
# THROW from there: 5 per move with 16 ms sleeps, released in place. Pass: release velocity within 1 pt/s of the speed
# over the last 0.1 s of the points as received; coast on the closed form within 0.01 pt; end = release + v*0.4995.
# The macOS file throws first and holds where the throw stopped; that place varies with the throw, and the hold missed
# the card on both Windows backends (2026-10-19), hence this order. Mouseups go in place: with a position, the
# synthesiser's move and checks delayed the release past the 0.1 s the velocity is measured over.
# 2026-10-19 Windows GTK: HOLD passes (20.00, velocity 0); the THROW drags the card to 70.00 but reads 0 pt/s -- the points arrive about 78 ms apart, and the 0.1 s velocity window holds none. Open.
# 2026-10-20: passes. The 78 ms was the replay, not GTK: each held move enumerated and (under --debug) dumped every window. Win32Synthesiser now keeps the pressed window while a button is held; points arrive 31-39 ms apart, THROW reads 106-128 pt/s and coasts on the closed form, err 0.
# 2026-10-20:通過。78 毫秒來自重放而非 GTK:每次按住移動都列舉(在 --debug 下還傾印)所有視窗;現在按住期間沿用按下時的視窗，點間隔 31-39 毫秒,THROW 讀到 106-128 pt/s 並依閉式解滑行。
